              <div class="surface__desc">
                <p>
                  We wrote <code>verify-astrolabe</code> to check our own work, and it lives in this
                  repository with our other skills. It names the tests that cover each feature, starts a
                  dev server on a clean home, and walks the feature in the app’s Browser panel.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Type <code>$</code> in the composer to list the skills your agent loads, each marked with
                  where it comes from. Pick one and send. The agent runs it as it would in its own command
                  line, and Astrolabe’s wiki, canvas and code tools are there for it to call.
                </p>
                <p class="surface__note">
                  Skills come from where each agent keeps them, such as <code>.claude/skills</code> for
                  Claude Code, and Astrolabe lists them in the composer from there.
                </p>
